  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tanzania - Cashew Import</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a DGGF Start-up Loan Johnny Cashew Nederland BV will be able to process cashews in Tanzania together with local partner Mama Cashew and import the cashews for sale in Europe. Currently, almost 60% of all cashew nuts are produced in Africa, but then transported to Vietnam and India to have the cashew removed from the nut before the cashew comes to Europe. This means that the added value is not earned in Africa, with the result that farmers receive a low price for their product. In addition, the impact on the climate is irresponsible because the cashew nuts have to travel an extra 125,000 km to be removed from the skin. Johnny Cashew Nederland B.V.  is a starting company that calls for a Cashew(revo)lution! they will source the cashews from the farmers&apos; cooperative of 450 farmers through their local partner, after which they will extract the cashew from the nut and sort the cashews into different quality levels. The processing is done in the Mama Cashew facility by 600 women. In the Netherlands, the cashews are roasted and flavored.</narrative>
  </description>
